  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study - Mass Rapid Transit Jakarta Renewable Energy Initiative Feasibility Study, through Jacobs Engineering Group, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant funds a feasibility study to support PT Mass Rapid Transit Jakarta (MRT Jakarta) in assessing the viability of implementing a renewable energy initiative that would transition MRT Jakarta&apos;s power supply to renewable energy sources. The activity would examine the technical and economic feasibility of installing solar panels on rooftops across the rail system, accessing power from new renewable energy power plants in Indonesia, and implementing energy efficiency and storage projects with a goal of using 100% renewable energy for the rail system&apos;s operational needs by 2035.</narrative>
  </description>
